          "case_id": "ifeval-wikipedia-no-comma-000",
          "dimension": "instruction_following",
          "prompt": "Write a 300+ word summary of the wikipedia page \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raymond_III,_Count_of_Tripoli\". Do not use any commas and highlight at least 3 sections that has titles in markdown format, for example *highlighted section part 1*, *highlighted section part 2*, *highlighted section part 3*.",
          "final_answer": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a medieval noble who ruled the County of Tripoli during the high medieval period. His father was Raymond II Count of Tripoli. He was born in the castle of Tripoli around the early thirteenth century. In his youth he took part in military campaigns against Muslim forces in the Levant. The County of Tripoli lay on the northern coast of the eastern Mediterranean. It served as a buffer zone between Christian states and Muslim powers. Raymond III inherited responsibilities from his father at a time of political tension.\n\n*Early Life*\nRaymond III was born in the fortress of Tripoli around the early thirteenth century. His father was Raymond II Count of Tripoli. He received his first tutelage in the cathedral school of Tripoli. At a young age he accompanied his father on a pilgrimage to Jerusalem. He learned the customs of the crusader states and developed an interest in military affairs. He studied law under local jurists. He observed the daily life of soldiers in the garrison. His curiosity led him to explore trade routes with merchants from the sea.\n\n*Reign*\nDuring his reign he acted as a defender of the county against external threats. He negotiated alliances with neighboring lords and with the Latin Church. He led several expeditions against Muslim strongholds in the region of Syria and Palestine. His leadership was marked by strategic patience and by careful use of local resources. He maintained relations with the Kingdom of Jerusalem and with other crusader principalities. He organized defenses when sieges approached the capital. He used diplomacy to resolve disputes with neighboring lords. He ensured that tax collection followed customary rules.\n\n*Later Years*\nIn later years Raymond III devoted much of his time to administrative affairs in Tripoli. He supported the construction of fortifications and promoted trade with Italian maritime cities. He died in Tripoli in the mid fourteenth century leaving a legacy of stable governance. His memory was recalled by chroniclers who praised his prudence. He appointed trusted officials to oversee town maintenance. He encouraged artisans to improve building techniques. He recorded important events in a simple chronicle.",
