          "final_answer": "<think>\nWe need to parse the genetics problem.\n\nWe have a trait: widow's peak (dominant allele W) vs straight hairline (recessive allele w). The man is homozygous dominant WW. The woman is heterozygous Ww. They produce a zygote. Which allele combinations could occur in the zygote? Options: A. WW or ww; B. WW or Ww; C. WW only; D. Ww only.\n\nWe need to consider that each parent contributes one allele per gene. The man is WW, so he can only give a W allele. The woman is Ww, she can give either W or w. So the possible zygote genotypes are: W from father + W from mother = WW; or W from father + w from mother = Ww. So the possible allele combinations in the zygote are WW or Ww. That matches choice B.\n\nThus answer: B. Provide final answer: <letter> B.\n\nBut we need to think step by step in 2-4 sentences, then give final answer. So we can write something like:\n\n\"The father contributes only a dominant W allele because he is homozygous WW, while the mother, being heterozygous Ww, can contribute either W or w. Therefore the zygote will receive one allele from each parent, resulting in either WW (if the mother gives W) or Ww (if she gives w). Hence the possible genotypes are WW or Ww.\"\n\nThen final answer: <letter> B.\n\nThus output accordingly.\n</think>\nThe father contributes only a dominant W allele because he is homozygous WW, while the heterozygous mother can pass either her dominant W or recessive w allele; thus the zygote will receive one allele from each parent, giving either WW (if the mother gives W) or Ww (if she gives w). <letter> B</letter>",
