          "case_id": "math-custom-op-hash-028",
          "dimension": "math",
          "prompt": "For all real numbers $r$ and $s$, define the mathematical operation $\\#$ such that the following conditions apply: $r\\ \\#\\ 0 = r, r\\ \\#\\ s = s\\ \\#\\ r$, and $(r + 1)\\ \\#\\ s = (r\\ \\#\\ s) + s + 1$. What is the value of $11\\ \\#\\ 5$?",
          "final_answer": "The operation \\(\\#\\) is defined for all real numbers \\(r\\) and \\(s\\) by the conditions:\n\n- \\(r \\# 0 = r\\)\n- \\(r \\# s = s \\# r\\) (commutative)\n- \\((r+1) \\# s = (r \\# s) + s + 1\\)\n\nFrom the third condition, for fixed \\(s\\), the function \\(h_s(r)=r \\# s\\) satisfies  \n\\(h_s(r+1)=h_s(r)+s+1\\). With \\(h_s(0)=0\\# s = s\\) (by commutativity and the first condition), we obtain by induction  \n\\[\nh_s(r)=s + r(s+1)=rs+r+s.\n\\]\n\nThus for any real \\(r,s\\),  \n\\[\nr \\# s = rs + r + s = (r+1)(s+1)-1.\n\\]\n\nNow evaluate \\(11 \\# 5\\):  \n\\[\n11 \\# 5 = 11\\cdot5 + 11 + 5 = 55 + 11 + 5 = 71,\n\\]  \nor equivalently \\((11+1)(5+1)-1 = 12\\cdot6-1 = 72-1 = 71\\).\n\nTherefore, the value is \\(\\boxed{71}\\).",
