          "dimension": "math",
          "prompt": "For what values of $x$ is it true that $x^2 - 5x - 4 \\le 10$? Express your answer in interval notation.",
          "final_answer": "The inequality is \\(x^2 - 5x - 4 \\le 10\\). Bring all terms to one side:\n\n\\[\nx^2 - 5x - 4 - 10 \\le 0 \\implies x^2 - 5x - 14 \\le 0.\n\\]\n\nSolve the equation \\(x^2 - 5x - 14 = 0\\) by factoring:\n\n\\[\nx^2 - 5x - 14 = (x - 7)(x + 2) = 0 \\implies x = 7 \\text{ or } x = -2.\n\\]\n\nThe quadratic opens upward, so the inequality \\(x^2 - 5x - 14 \\le 0\\) holds for \\(x\\) between the roots, inclusive:\n\n\\[\n-2 \\le x \\le 7.\n\\]\n\nIn interval notation, this is \\([-2, 7]\\).\n\n\\boxed{[-2, 7]}",
