          "case_id": "humaneval-paren-groups-001",
          "dimension": "coding",
          "prompt": "from typing import List\n\n\ndef separate_paren_groups(paren_string: str) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\" Input to this function is a string containing multiple groups of nested parentheses. Your goal is to\n    separate those group into separate strings and return the list of those.\n    Separate groups are balanced (each open brace is properly closed) and not nested within each other\n    Ignore any spaces in the input string.\n    >>> separate_paren_groups('( ) (( )) (( )( ))')\n    ['()', '(())', '(()())']\n    \"\"\"",
          "final_answer": "To solve this problem, we need to separate a given string containing multiple groups of balanced parentheses into individual strings. Each group is defined as a balanced sequence of parentheses and should not be nested within another group. The solution should ignore any spaces in the input string.\n\n### Approach\n1. **Remove Spaces**: First, we remove all spaces from the input string to simplify processing.\n2. **Iterate Through Characters**: We iterate through each character in the cleaned string.\n3. **Track Current Group**: We maintain a list to collect characters of the current group. When an opening parenthesis '(' is encountered, we start a new group. When a closing parenthesis ')' is encountered, we end the current group.\n4. **Collect Groups**: Each time we encounter an opening parenthesis, we start a new group. When we encounter a closing parenthesis, we add the collected characters of the current group to the result list and reset the current group.\n5. **Return Result**: After processing all characters, the result list contains all the balanced groups, which we return.\n\n### Solution Code\n```python\nfrom typing import List\n\ndef separate_paren_groups(paren_string: str) -> List[str]:\n    # Remove all spaces from the input string\n    cleaned = paren_string.replace(' ', '')\n    result = []\n    current_group = []\n    \n    for char in cleaned:\n        if char == '(':\n            current_group.append(char)\n        elif char == ')':\n            current_group.append(char)\n            result.append(''.join(current_group))\n            current_group = []\n    \n    return result\n```\n\n### Explanation\n- **Removing Spaces**: The input string is cleaned to remove any spaces, ensuring that only parentheses are considered.\n- **Tracking Groups**: As we iterate through each character, we use a list `current_group` to collect characters of the current group. When an opening parenthesis '(' is encountered, it starts a new group. When a closing parenthesis ')' is encountered, the current group is completed, and the characters are added to the result list.\n- **Efficiency**: This approach efficiently processes each character exactly once, resulting in a time complexity of O(n), where n is the length of the input string. The space complexity is also O(n) in the worst case, where all characters form a single group.\n\nThis method ensures that each group of balanced parentheses is correctly separated and returned as a list of strings, ignoring any spaces in the input.",
