          "final_answer": "Fortune cookies have roots in Chinese culture, but the modern version was developed and popularized in the United States by Chinese immigrants in the early 20th century. While the concept of giving a \"fortune\" inside a treat may have existed in China, the specific cookie with a paper slip containing a message was created and sold in the U.S. starting around the 1920s–1930s. So, although they originated in China, they became iconic in American cuisine through the efforts of Chinese communities there.",
