          "dimension": "instruction_following",
          "prompt": "Write a 300+ word summary of the wikipedia page \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raymond_III,_Count_of_Tripoli\". Do not use any commas and highlight at least 3 sections that has titles in markdown format, for example *highlighted section part 1*, *highlighted section part 2*, *highlighted section part 3*.",
          "final_answer": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a member of the House of Toulouse and the Count of Tripoli from 1152 until his death in 1187. He was the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem. Raymond III was a key figure in the Crusader states and played a significant role in the politics of the region.\n\n**Early Life and Reign**\n\nRaymond III was born around 1140 and succeeded his father as Count of Tripoli in 1152. He was a minor at the time and his mother Hodierna acted as regent until he came of age. During his early years as count Raymond III faced several challenges including the threat of the Zengid dynasty and the internal conflicts within the Crusader states.\n\n**Relationship with the Kingdom of Jerusalem**\n\nRaymond III had a close relationship with the Kingdom of Jerusalem and often worked closely with its rulers. He was a key ally of King Amalric I of Jerusalem and supported him in his campaigns against the Fatimid Caliphate. Raymond III also married Eschiva of Bures a member of the noble family of Bures in 1160. The marriage was likely arranged to strengthen the ties between the County of Tripoli and the Kingdom of Jerusalem.\n\n**Military Campaigns and Death**\n\nRaymond III was involved in several military campaigns during his reign including the Battle of Montgisard in 1177 and the Battle of Marj Ayyun in 1179. He also played a key role in the defense of the Crusader states against the Ayyubid dynasty. Raymond III died in 1187 during the Battle of Hattin and was succeeded by his son Bohemond IV of Antioch.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nRaymond III's legacy is complex and multifaceted. He was a skilled diplomat and military leader who played a significant role in the politics of the Crusader states. However his reign was also marked by internal conflicts and external threats. Despite these challenges Raymond III remained a key figure in the region until his death in 1187.",
