          "final_answer": "\"MATTHIAS ALGIERS\nSenior Product Designer | San Francisco, CA\n\nCONTACT\nmatthias.algiers@email.com · +1 (555) 014-2278\n\nPROFILE\nProduct designer with eight years of experience creating clear, useful interfaces for teams that ship fast. Matthias combines research, systems thinking, and hands-on prototyping to turn complex problems into products people understand.\n\nEXPERIENCE\n\nSenior Product Designer — Northstar Health (2021–Present)\n- Led the redesign of a patient scheduling platform used by 40,000 members each month.\n- Built a shared component library that reduced design-to-development handoff time by 35 percent.\n- Partnered with clinical operations to map workflows and validate changes through usability testing.\n\nProduct Designer — Lumen Analytics (2018–2021)\n- Owned the reporting experience for a B2B analytics platform serving 600 enterprise accounts.\n- Introduced data visualization patterns that cut time-to-insight for weekly reports by half.\n- Facilitated design critiques across four product teams.\n\nJunior Designer — Fieldwork Studio (2016–2018)\n- Produced brand systems, marketing sites, and presentation decks for early-stage companies.\n- Ran user interviews and translated findings into interface concepts.\n\nEDUCATION\nBFA Interaction Design, California College of the Arts, 2016\n\nCORE STRENGTHS\nResearch · Prototyping · Design systems · Accessibility · Stakeholder communication\n\nSELECTED WORK\n- Patient scheduling platform for a regional health network (2023)\n- Reporting dashboard used by 600 enterprise accounts (2021)\n- Brand and web system for three early-stage companies (2017–2018)\"",
