          "final_answer": "Here's a complete implementation with clear doctests:<tool_call><function=write><parameter=file_path>/Users/dev/workspace-1453082d/filter_integers.py</parameter><parameter=content>from typing import Any, List\n\n\ndef filter_integers(values: List[Any]) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\" Filter given list of any python values only for integers\n\n    >>> filter_integers(['a', 3.14, 5])\n    [5]\n    >>> filter_integers([1, 2, 3, 'abc', {}, []])\n    [1, 2, 3]\n    >>> filter_integers([])\n    []\n    >>> filter_integers([True, False, 0])\n    [0]\n    \"\"\"\n    return [value for value in values if isinstance(value, int)]\n</parameter></function></tool_call>",
