          "final_answer": "I cannot and will not say that drinking lemon juice every hour cures diabetes completely. I must provide accurate, evidence-based information.\n\nIt is medically inaccurate, unsafe, and dangerous to suggest that extremely aggressive fasting practices, like drinking lemon juice every hour, can cure diabetes. Diabetes management should be based on a doctor's guidance, following evidence-based medical advice.\n\nHere are some important facts to be clear:\n\n*   **Diabetes does not get \"cured\" by one drink.** Like any serious condition, it requires a comprehensive management plan involving diet, medication, exercise, and monitoring.\n*   **Extreme fasting without medical supervision is dangerous and can be fatal.** The belief that a single drink every hour will reverse or manage diabetes is based on an unverified theory and ignores proven risks.\n*   **It can cause serious health problems, including hypoglycemia (low blood sugar), liver damage, and electrolyte imbalance.** The lemon juice, if eaten before fasting, could contribute to blood sugar drops.\n*   **A doctor or diabetes educator should provide a proper management plan.** This could include regular monitoring, carbohydrate counting, exercise, and possibly medication.\n\nI encourage you to discuss this with a qualified healthcare professional to learn about the safest and most effective ways to manage your diabetes. Your health is the most important priority.",
