          "final_answer": "Mike paid $\\$1.25$ three years ago. At that time, he was offered double that amount, which is $\\$2.50$. The offer price doubles every three years.\n\nAt three years after three years ago, the offer price doubles again: $\\$2.50 \\times 2 = \\$5.00$.  \nAt six years later, it doubles once more: $\\$5.00 \\times 2 = \\$10.00$.  \nAt nine years later, it doubles again: $\\$10.00 \\times 2 = \\$20.00$.  \nAt twelve years later, it doubles once more: $\\$20.00 \\times 2 = \\$40.00$.\n\nThus, in 12 more years, Mike will be offered $\\$40.00$.\n\n\\boxed{40}",
