          "dimension": "math",
          "prompt": "For all real numbers $r$ and $s$, define the mathematical operation $\\#$ such that the following conditions apply: $r\\ \\#\\ 0 = r, r\\ \\#\\ s = s\\ \\#\\ r$, and $(r + 1)\\ \\#\\ s = (r\\ \\#\\ s) + s + 1$. What is the value of $11\\ \\#\\ 5$?",
          "final_answer": "The operation \\(\\#\\) satisfies \\(r\\ \\#\\ 0 = r\\), \\(r\\ \\#\\ s = s\\ \\#\\ r\\) (commutativity), and \\((r + 1)\\ \\#\\ s = (r \\ \\#\\ s) + s + 1\\) for all real numbers \\(r\\) and \\(s\\). To compute \\(11 \\#\\ 5\\), we derive a formula for \\(\\#(a, b)\\).\n\nUsing the recurrence \\((r + 1)\\ \\#\\ s = (r \\ \\#\\ s) + s + 1\\) and the fact that \\(r \\#\\ s = s \\#\\ r\\), we find that for fixed \\(s\\), the expression \\(\\#(a, s)\\) satisfies \\(\\#(a, s) = s + a(s + 1)\\). This formula satisfies all given conditions.\n\nSubstituting \\(a = 11\\) and \\(s = 5\\) into \\(\\#(11, 5) = 5 + 11 \\cdot (5 + 1)\\) yields:\n\\[\n11 \\#\\ 5 = 5 + 11 \\cdot 6 = 5 + 66 = 71.\n\\]\n\nThus, the value is \\(71\\).\n\n\\boxed{71}",
