          "case_id": "ifeval-three-bullets-005",
          "dimension": "instruction_following",
          "prompt": "Write a dialogue between two people, one is dressed up in a ball gown and the other is dressed down in sweats. The two are going to a nightly event. Your answer must contain exactly 3 bullet points in the markdown format (use \"* \" to indicate each bullet) such as:\n* This is the first point.\n* This is the second point.",
          "final_answer": "**Scene:** Café – Evening\n\n*Me! Ball gown tonight! Can't miss this nightly event—it's an absolute must!*\n\n*He looks at his sweats with resigned dignity.* (*A guy in comfortable sweats*)\n\n*Yeah, totally defeatist. My sweats are like a tiny time machine—I can go to a place whenever I want.*\n\n*I don't care. Think about it—overdressed once and you know what happens. It starts something, doesn't it?*\n\n*He nods slowly, adjusting his t-shirt.* (*A guy in comfortable sweats)\n\n*It's not just about the outfit though. It's about the energy.* (*Ball gown girl)\n\n*Exactly! My ball gown is my confidence amplifier!*\n\n*He gives a skeptical, then genuine, nod.* (*A guy in comfortable sweats)\n\n*Alright! Let's go there!*\n\n*He says—but first he asks me if I'll check the dress hemline again.* (*Ball gown girl)\n\n*Just once!* (*Sweats guy smiles*)\n\n*Right. Always-on standby!*\n\n*Ball gown girl:* Nightly events don't discriminate! *He: (beat)* Okay, but I'll bring my mask—I prefer to prepare for the after party.*\n\n*Ball gown girl:* (laughs) You again! But the vibe is already locked in!\n\n**Dialogue ends. Here are the three key takeaways:**\n\n* The ball gown girl represents how external presentation can fuel inner confidence, suggesting that dressing up is ultimately a performance for oneself rather than for others.\n\n* The sweats guy embodies self-acceptance redefined—the idea that being comfortable in your own skin isn't rejecting a night out but embracing a different kind of participation that prioritizes authenticity over convention.\n\n* Their complementary styles reveal that the value of the \"nightly event\" lies not in matching outfits but in mutual support, where one celebrates boldness and the other offers practicality—both valid expressions of enjoyment.",
