          "case_id": "math-ceiling-fraction-002",
          "dimension": "math",
          "prompt": "Find $x$ such that $\\lceil x \\rceil + x = \\dfrac{23}{7}$. Express $x$ as a common fraction.",
          "final_answer": "Given the equation $\\lceil x \\rceil + x = \\frac{23}{7}$, let $n = \\lceil x \\rceil$. Then $n + x = \\frac{23}{7}$, so $x = \\frac{23}{7} - n$.\n\nSince $\\lceil x \\rceil = n$, we have $n - 1 < x \\leq n$, and because $n$ is an integer and $\\frac{23}{14} \\approx 1.64$, $\\frac{15}{7} \\approx 2.14$, the only possible integer value is $n = 2$.\n\nThus, $x = \\frac{23}{7} - 2 = \\frac{9}{7}$.\n\nChecking: $\\lceil \\frac{9}{7} \\rceil = 2$, and $2 + \\frac{9}{7} = \\frac{23}{7}$. The solution is valid.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{9}{7}}\n\\]",
