          "case_id": "math-prime-roots-020",
          "dimension": "math",
          "prompt": "Suppose the roots of the polynomial $x^2 - mx + n$ are positive prime integers (not necessarily distinct). Given that $m < 20,$ how many possible values of $n$ are there?",
