          "final_answer": "To determine how much Mike will be offered for his stamp in 12 more years, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Identify the current offer price:**\n   - Three years ago, the stamp was offered for $1.25.\n   - The offer price doubles every three years.\n   - Since three years have already passed, the offer price will double again in the next three years.\n\n2. **Calculate the offer price after the next three years:**\n   - The current offer price is $1.25.\n   - Doubling this price gives:\n     \\[\n     1.25 \\times 2 = 2.50\n     \\]\n\n3. **calculate the offer price after the next 12 years:**\n   - The offer price will double again in the next three years.\n   - Doubling $2.50 gives:\n     \\[\n     2.50 \\times 2 = 5.00\n     \\]\n\nTherefore, in 12 more years, Mike will be offered \\(\\boxed{5.00}\\) dollars for his stamp.",
