          "final_answer": "Here is the step-by-step calculation to determine the offer price:\n\n1.  **Identify the current offer:**\n    Mike paid $\\$1.25$ three years ago. The problem states he was just offered double that amount.\n    $$ \\$1.25 \\times 2 = \\$2.50 $$\n    So, the current offer is $\\$2.50$.\n\n2.  **Determine the number of doubling periods:**\n    The price doubles every three years. We need to find the price in 12 more years.\n    $$ \\frac{12 \\text{ years}}{3 \\text{ years per period}} = 4 \\text{ periods} $$\n\n3.  **Calculate the final price:**\n    We need to double the current offer ($\\$2.50$) four times.\n    $$ \\$2.50 \\times 2^4 $$\n    $$ \\$2.50 \\times 16 $$\n    $$ \\$40.00 $$\n\nHe will be offered **$\\$40$**.",
