          "case_id": "humaneval-make-palindrome-010",
          "dimension": "coding",
          "prompt": "\n\ndef is_palindrome(string: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\" Test if given string is a palindrome \"\"\"\n    return string == string[::-1]\n\n\ndef make_palindrome(string: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\" Find the shortest palindrome that begins with a supplied string.\n    Algorithm idea is simple:\n    - Find the longest postfix of supplied string that is a palindrome.\n    - Append to the end of the string reverse of a string prefix that comes before the palindromic suffix.\n    >>> make_palindrome('')\n    ''\n    >>> make_palindrome('cat')\n    'catac'\n    >>> make_palindrome('cata')\n    'catac'\n    \"\"\"\n",
          "final_answer": "```python\ndef is_palindrome(string: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\" Test if given string is a palindrome \"\"\"\n    return string == string[::-1]\n\n\ndef make_palindrome(string: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\" Find the shortest palindrome that begins with a supplied string.\n    Algorithm idea is simple:\n    - Find the longest postfix of supplied string that is a palindrome.\n    - Append to the end of the string reverse of a string prefix that comes before the palindromic suffix.\n    >>> make_palindrome('')\n    ''\n    >>> make_palindrome('cat')\n    'catac'\n    >>> make_palindrome('cata')\n    'catac'\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(string)\n    \n    # Find the longest palindromic suffix\n    for i in range(n):\n        suffix = string[i:]\n        if is_palindrome(suffix):\n            prefix = string[:i]\n            return string + prefix[::-1]\n    \n    return string\n```\n\n### Explanation:\n\nThe function `make_palindrome` constructs the shortest palindrome that starts with the given input string by identifying the longest palindromic suffix and appending the reverse of the remaining prefix.\n\n- It iterates through all possible suffixes starting from index 0 to n−1.\n- For each suffix, it checks if it is a palindrome using `is_palindrome`.\n- Once the longest palindromic suffix is found, it reverses the preceding prefix and appends it to the original string.\n- If no non-empty suffix is palindromic (e.g., input is empty), it returns the original string unchanged.\n\n### Example Walkthroughs:\n\n1. `make_palindrome('cat')`  \n   - Suffixes: `'t'`, `'at'`, `'cat'`  \n   - Longest palindromic suffix: `'t'`  \n   - Prefix before it: `'ca'` → reversed: `'ac'`  \n   - Result: `'cat' + 'ac' = 'catac'`\n\n2. `make_palindrome('cata')`  \n   - Suffixes: `'a'`, `'ta'`, `'ata'`, `'cata'`  \n   - Longest palindromic suffix: `'ata'`  \n   - Prefix before it: `'c'` → reversed: `'c'`  \n   - Result: `'cata' + 'c' = 'catac'`\n\n3. `make_palindrome('')`  \n   - No characters to process  \n   - Returns: `''`\n\n### Complexity:\n- Time: O(n²) — due to repeated palindrome checks on substrings of length up to n.\n- Space: O(n) — for storing substrings and reversed prefix.",
